@* Badge (UI docs): the badge and the status dot. Sections: Usage, Examples, Customization, Styling reference, API,
   Accessibility, Guidelines. *@

<ul class="dnf-docs-source">
    <li>CSS <code>src/DotNetForge.UI/Styles/components/status.css</code></li>
    <li>Tag helpers <code>&lt;dnf-badge&gt;</code> and <code>&lt;dnf-status-dot&gt;</code> in <code>src/DotNetForge.UI/Components/BasicTagHelpers.cs</code></li>
</ul>

<h2 id="usage">Usage</h2>
<p>A badge is a small pill of text that tells a status or a kind: Published, Draft, Failed, GET. Use the
    <code>&lt;dnf-badge&gt;</code> tag helper or the classes on a <code>&lt;span&gt;</code>.</p>

<ui-doc-example id="basic">
    <dnf-badge tone="Success" dot="true">Published</dnf-badge>
    <span class="dnf-badge">Draft</span>
</ui-doc-example>

<h2 id="examples">Examples</h2>

<ui-doc-example id="tones" title="Tones" description="Neutral (the default), Success, Warning, Danger, Info and Primary: a soft background in the tone's colour.">
    <dnf-badge>Neutral</dnf-badge>
    <dnf-badge tone="Success">Success</dnf-badge>
    <dnf-badge tone="Warning">Warning</dnf-badge>
    <dnf-badge tone="Danger">Danger</dnf-badge>
    <dnf-badge tone="Info">Info</dnf-badge>
    <dnf-badge tone="Primary">Primary</dnf-badge>
</ui-doc-example>

<ui-doc-example id="dot" title="With a dot" description="A leading dot in the text colour marks a status (on, off, failing) rather than a category.">
    <dnf-badge tone="Success" dot="true">Enabled</dnf-badge>
    <dnf-badge dot="true">Disabled</dnf-badge>
    <dnf-badge tone="Warning" dot="true">Retrying</dnf-badge>
    <dnf-badge tone="Danger" dot="true">Failing</dnf-badge>
</ui-doc-example>

<ui-doc-example id="outline" title="Outline" description="Transparent with a border - quieter, for labels next to other badges.">
    <dnf-badge outline="true">Default</dnf-badge>
    <dnf-badge outline="true" tone="Primary">Beta</dnf-badge>
    <dnf-badge outline="true" tone="Danger">Deprecated</dnf-badge>
</ui-doc-example>

<ui-doc-example id="mono" title="Monospace" description="mono (dnf-badge--mono) for HTTP methods, status codes and versions.">
    <dnf-badge tone="Info" mono="true">GET</dnf-badge>
    <dnf-badge tone="Success" mono="true">POST</dnf-badge>
    <dnf-badge tone="Danger" mono="true">DELETE</dnf-badge>
    <span class="dnf-badge dnf-badge--outline dnf-badge--mono">v1.4.0</span>
</ui-doc-example>

<ui-doc-example id="in-text" title="Next to text" description="A badge sits on the text's middle, in headings, table cells and list rows.">
    <span class="font-semibold">Newsletter webhook</span>
    <dnf-badge tone="Success" dot="true">Enabled</dnf-badge>
</ui-doc-example>

<ui-doc-example id="status-dot" title="Status dot" description="A dot without text, with an accessible name that is also its tooltip - for tight places such as a tree or a narrow column.">
    <dnf-status-dot tone="Success" label="Published" />
    <dnf-status-dot tone="Warning" label="Scheduled" />
    <dnf-status-dot tone="Danger" label="Failed" />
    <dnf-status-dot tone="Info" label="Syncing" />
    <dnf-status-dot tone="Primary" label="Current" />
    <dnf-status-dot label="Draft" />
</ui-doc-example>

<h2 id="customization">Customization</h2>
<p>The three <a href="@UiDocsCatalog.Root/customization">customization levels</a>, none needing <code>!important</code>.</p>

<ui-doc-example id="custom-tailwind" title="Tailwind utilities" description="A class on the tag helper is appended to the badge's own classes.">
    <dnf-badge tone="Primary" class="uppercase tracking-wide">New</dnf-badge>
    <dnf-badge class="rounded-sm">Square</dnf-badge>
</ui-doc-example>

<ui-doc-example id="custom-tokens" title="Component tokens" description="Every tone only sets --dnf-badge-background and --dnf-badge-foreground; set them in your own (unlayered) CSS to recolour badges in a scope.">
    <div class="dnf-docs-demo-badges dnf-cluster">
        <dnf-badge>Neutral</dnf-badge>
        <dnf-badge tone="Success" dot="true">Restyled</dnf-badge>
    </div>
</ui-doc-example>

<ui-doc-code id="custom-tokens-css" lang="css">
.dnf-docs-demo-badges .dnf-badge {
    --dnf-badge-background: var(--dnf-surface);
    box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px var(--dnf-border-strong);
}
</ui-doc-code>

<h2 id="styling">Styling reference</h2>
<h3 id="classes">Classes</h3>
<table>
    <thead><tr><th>Class</th><th>Kind</th><th>Effect</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>dnf-badge</code></td><td>block</td><td>a 1.375rem pill, <code>text-xs</code>, semibold, no wrap; neutral (muted surface and text) by default</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>dnf-badge--success</code>, <code>--warning</code>, <code>--danger</code>, <code>--info</code>, <code>--primary</code></td><td>tone</td><td>the tone's soft background and colour (primary uses <code>--dnf-primary-text</code>)</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>dnf-badge--outline</code></td><td>modifier</td><td>transparent with an inset border</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>dnf-badge--mono</code></td><td>modifier</td><td>monospace (HTTP methods, codes)</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>dnf-badge--dot</code></td><td>modifier</td><td>a leading dot in the text colour</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>dnf-status-dot</code></td><td>block</td><td>a 0.5rem dot in <code>--dnf-subtle-foreground</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>dnf-status-dot--success</code>, <code>--warning</code>, <code>--danger</code>, <code>--info</code>, <code>--primary</code></td><td>tone</td><td>the tone's colour</td></tr>
    </tbody>
</table>

<h3 id="tokens">Tokens</h3>
<p><code>--dnf-badge-background</code> and <code>--dnf-badge-foreground</code>, on <code>dnf-badge</code>. The status dot has none.</p>

<h2 id="api">API</h2>
<h3 id="api-badge"><code>&lt;dnf-badge&gt;</code></h3>
<ui-doc-api type="typeof(DotNetForge.UI.Components.DnfBadgeTagHelper)" />
<p>Renders a <code>&lt;span&gt;</code> around the content. <code>Neutral</code> adds no tone modifier. Other attributes pass
    through; <code>class</code> is appended.</p>

<h3 id="api-status-dot"><code>&lt;dnf-status-dot&gt;</code></h3>
<ui-doc-api type="typeof(DotNetForge.UI.Components.DnfStatusDotTagHelper)" />
<p>A self-closing element that renders an empty <code>&lt;span role="img"&gt;</code> with <code>aria-label</code> and
    <code>data-tooltip</code> set to the label. Without a label it is <code>aria-hidden="true"</code> decoration - then the
    status must be written in nearby text.</p>

<h2 id="accessibility">Accessibility</h2>
<ul>
    <li>A badge is text: the word carries the meaning, the colour only supports it.</li>
    <li>A status dot has no text - always give it a <code>label</code> (the tag helper turns it into <code>role="img"</code>, an <code>aria-label</code> and a tooltip).</li>
</ul>

<h2 id="guidelines">Guidelines</h2>
<ul>
    <li>Do use the tone that matches the meaning: success for working or published, warning for attention, danger for failed or blocked.</li>
    <li>Do keep badge text to one or two words.</li>
    <li>Don't make badges clickable; use a <a href="@UiDocsCatalog.Root/components/chip">chip</a> or a button.</li>
    <li>Don't use a status dot where there is room for a badge - text is clearer than a colour.</li>
</ul>
